# Line endings.
#
# The repository already stores text with LF, and biome — which the Checks
# workflow and the pre-push hook both run — formats to LF. On Windows,
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites files to CRLF whenever git touches them, so an
# ordinary checkout, pull, or merge leaves source that biome then rejects, and
# the push is blocked by a formatting error on a file nobody edited.
#
# Pinning the checkout to LF makes a working tree on any platform match both
# what the repository stores and what the formatter expects.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything whose bytes must survive verbatim.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.wasm binary
*.docx binary
